   "slug": "combat",
   "title": "Combat, buffs & recovery",
   "summary": "Casting, lasting buffs and getting back into the world.",
-  "body": "<h2 id=\"buffs\">Lasting blessings and temporary abilities</h2><p>Ordinary beneficial blessings on you and your owned pets persist without timer upkeep. Temporary AA effects, including Killing Spree and related triggered buffs, disciplines and short-duration song-window effects retain their timers. Death, dispels, replacement, stacking rules, charges and aura range still matter. Debuffs and hostile NPC buffs keep their timers.</p>\n<h2 id=\"bard-songs\">Bard songs and effect duration</h2><p>Song-window effects keep their normal timers; do not assume every beneficial song is permanent. Harmful effects such as damage, charm and mez keep their normal rules. Movement-song behavior is still being checked.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blessing-repair\">Blessing effects that survive reconnects</h2><p>Repairs restore saved buff effects after login and stop permanent blessings expiring on the next tick. You should not need another hail or payment; player retesting continues.</p>\n<h2 id=\"casting\">Instant damage-over-time casts</h2><p>Your damage-over-time spells cast instantly, while keeping mana costs, target and resistance checks, and reuse limits. Direct-damage spells keep their normal cast times.</p>\n<h2 id=\"melee-casting\">Melee attacks during casting</h2><p>Main-hand and offhand autoattacks can continue while you cast. Range, stuns, fear, and other control effects still apply.</p>\n<h2 id=\"death-recovery\">Keep your belongings after death</h2><p>Return to your bind point with equipment, inventory, and money. You still lose beneficial buffs; other death rules are unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"throw-stone\">Throw Stone and Spell Damage</h2><p>Throw Stone now adds effective Spell Damage directly. At 250 Spell Damage, it deals 251 ordinary damage before other modifiers. Encounter balance remains under testing.</p><h2 id=\"spell-gems\">Spell gems after death</h2><p>Memorized spell gems now persist through normal death. Death and reconnect testing is still ongoing.</p><h2 id=\"healing\">Heal yourself while keeping an enemy targeted</h2><p>Ordinary heals cast with an NPC or pet selected heal you while keeping that target selected. Select another player to heal them. Pet-only and other specialized spells retain their target rules.</p><h2 id=\"food-drink\">Food and drink are optional</h2><p>Hunger and thirst no longer penalize recovery, and ordinary food/drink consumption no longer removes those items. Optional food bonuses, crafting ingredients and alcohol keep their own uses. Sell All preserves food, drink and spell supplies.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Not released:</strong> Removing the EXP penalty from normal death is prepared for approval. It is not active yet. <a href=\"unreleased.html#death-exp\">See the candidate details.</a></p>",
+  "body": "<h2 id=\"buffs\">Lasting blessings and temporary abilities</h2><p>Ordinary beneficial blessings on you and your owned pets persist without timer upkeep. Temporary AA effects, including Killing Spree and related triggered buffs, disciplines and short-duration song-window effects retain their timers. Death, dispels, replacement, stacking rules, charges and aura range still matter. Debuffs and hostile NPC buffs keep their timers.</p>\n<h2 id=\"bard-songs\">Bard songs and effect duration</h2><p>Song-window effects keep their normal timers; do not assume every beneficial song is permanent. Harmful effects such as damage, charm and mez keep their normal rules. Movement-song behavior is still being checked.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blessing-repair\">Blessing effects that survive reconnects</h2><p>Repairs restore saved buff effects after login and stop permanent blessings expiring on the next tick. You should not need another hail or payment; player retesting continues.</p>\n<h2 id=\"casting\">Instant damage-over-time casts</h2><p>Your damage-over-time spells cast instantly, while keeping mana costs, target and resistance checks, and reuse limits. Direct-damage spells keep their normal cast times.</p>\n<h2 id=\"melee-casting\">Melee attacks during casting</h2><p>Main-hand and offhand autoattacks can continue while you cast. Range, stuns, fear, and other control effects still apply.</p>\n<h2 id=\"death-recovery\">Keep your belongings after death</h2><p>Return to your bind point with equipment, inventory, and money. You still lose beneficial buffs; other death rules are unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"throw-stone\">Throw Stone and Spell Damage</h2><p>Throw Stone now adds effective Spell Damage directly. At 250 Spell Damage, it deals 251 ordinary damage before other modifiers. Encounter balance remains under testing.</p><h2 id=\"spell-gems\">Spell gems after death</h2><p>Memorized spell gems now persist through normal death. Death and reconnect testing is still ongoing.</p><h2 id=\"healing\">Heal yourself while keeping an enemy targeted</h2><p>Ordinary heals cast with an NPC or pet selected heal you while keeping that target selected. Select another player to heal them. Pet-only and other specialized spells retain their target rules.</p><h2 id=\"food-drink\">Food and drink are optional</h2><p>Hunger and thirst no longer penalize recovery, and ordinary food/drink consumption no longer removes those items. Optional food bonuses, crafting ingredients and alcohol keep their own uses. Sell All preserves food, drink and spell supplies.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Not released:</strong> Removing the EXP penalty from normal death is prepared for approval. It is not active yet. <a href=\"unreleased.html#death-exp\">See the candidate details.</a></p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Not released:</strong> Separate cooldowns for the six basic Monk attacks are prepared. Dragon Punch/Tail Rake, Eagle Strike, Flying Kick, Kick, Round Kick and Tiger Claw will each keep their own reuse time. <a href=\"unreleased.html#monk-cooldowns\">See the candidate details.</a></p>",
