ppear in Actions → Abilities and can be assigned to hotbuttons. Extra-class Monk attacks, disciplines and dual wield use your held-class eligibility and native requirements. Owning a class does not grant maximum skill.</p>\n<h2 id=\"passive-abilities\">20% passive AA while leveling</h2><p>With ability focus off, eligible kills and quest/task rewards give full normal leveling experience plus <strong>20% of their full ability-experience award</strong>. Nothing is taken away from leveling. The live rate changed from 40% to 20% on October 13. Tiny awards can round down; saved progress carries toward the next point. The current conversion is <strong>4,000 AA experience per point</strong>; ability purchase prices still vary.</p>\n<h2 id=\"alternate-abilities\">Allowed AA ranks open at level 1</h2><p>Every rank in Nightcap’s allowed AA pool is available from level 1. Your held classes, eligibility, prerequisite ranks and earned points still govern purchases; this is not unrestricted access to every EverQuest AA.</p><p>Use <code>#aaexp off</code> for normal leveling plus passive ability gains, or <code>#aaexp on</code> to send eligible experience entirely to abilities. Full focus receives no additional passive bonus. Partial allocations become 100%. Use <code>#aaexp</code> to check your setting.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ability-class-column\">A Class column in the ability window</h2><p>The ability window identifies class origins in a dedicated Class column across its four tabs, making a multiclass build easier to browse.</p>\n<h2 id=\"class-release\">Extra-class changes and ability refunds</h2><p>The Chronicler can remove an extra class, refund eligible earned ability points, and adjust skill limits. Shared abilities and scribed spells remain; your remaining classes govern spell use. <strong class=\"inline\">Try a spare character first while this is being tested.</strong></p>\n<h2 id=\"starter-provisions\">A useful starting kit</h2><p>New characters begin in the tunnel with 100 platinum, a starting-class weapon, and a robe with 10 armor class and +5 to their main stat. These are one-time creation rewards.</p>\n\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Not released:</strong> Removing the EXP penalty from normal death is prepared for approval. It is not active yet. <a href=\"unreleased.html#death-exp\">See the candidate details.</a></p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Not released:</strong> Separate cooldowns for the six basic Monk attacks are prepared. Dragon Punch/Tail Rake, Eagle Strike, Flying Kick, Kick, Round Kick and Tiger Claw will each keep their own reuse time. <a href=\"unreleased.html#monk-cooldowns\">See the candidate details.</a></p>",
