oic stats.</p><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">Explore rewards and sockets →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Turn duplicates into upgrades</h3><div><p>Use three Base zone rewards for Polished, then four matching copies for each higher step. Veyra’s reusable box also upgrades eligible ordinary Polished and Exalted items. A <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three-Normal-to-Polished box update</a> is awaiting release.</p><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">See the upgrade recipes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Free trading and no LORE limit</h3><div><p>Trade formerly restricted and attuned items and keep duplicate LORE items. Inventory space, temporary lifetime and other item rules still apply.</p><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">Read trading and resale rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Equipment for your held classes</h3><div><p>Wear ordinary equipment allowed by any held class, regardless of playable race. Other restrictions, including slot, level and deity, remain.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Check equipment eligibility →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"adventuring\">Prepare in the tunnel, then explore</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Raid or Grind in seven private dungeons</h3><div><p>Choose normal respawning enemies or harder enemies with permanent deaths. Earn personal boss-checklist rewards; Raid final bosses add exclusive loot.</p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Choose your dungeon mode →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A shared home base</h3><div><p>New characters start with a kit and 100 platinum in the East Commonlands tunnel. Trainers, spell shops, supplies, banking, buffs and travel services are gathered there.</p><a href=\"tunnel.html\">Meet the tunnel services →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Travel, discovery and private dungeons</h3><div><p>Use tunnel travel services, discover waypoint destinations and enter supported personal dungeon instances. Ancient Attunement recalls you home without changing your bind.</p><a href=\"travel.html\">Plan your journey →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Lasting blessings; temporary combat abilities</h3><div><p>Ordinary beneficial blessings persist on players and owned pets. Temporary AA effects, disciplines and short-duration effects retain their timers.</p><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Know which effects last →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Keep fighting while you cast</h3><div><p>Damage-over-time spells cast instantly, and melee autoattacks can continue during casting. Mana costs, reuse, resistance and control effects still matter.</p><a href=\"combat.html#casting\">Read the combat changes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Less upkeep between adventures</h3><div><p>Food and drink are optional. Normal death retains carried equipment, inventory, money and memorized spell gems; beneficial buffs are lost. Preparation, earned gear and encounter execution still matter.</p><a href=\"combat.html\">Read combat and recovery →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Healing without changing your target</h3><div><p>Ordinary heals cast with an enemy or pet selected heal you. Select a player to heal them; specialized and pet-only spells keep their own rules.</p><a href=\"combat.html#healing\">Check healing targets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"tools\">Spend more time playing</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stacked materials and Craft All</h3><div><p>Use stacks without manually splitting every ingredient. Repeat a recipe with Craft All while retaining normal recipe requirements, success chances and skill gains.</p><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Use the crafting controls →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Advanced loot and bulk selling</h3><div><p>Use personal loot queues, loot preferences and group rolls. Sell All keeps bags and casting supplies; bank valuable gear before selling.</p><a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Learn the loot interface →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>One launcher, current updates</h3><div><p>The normal Nightcap shortcut delivers managed game/interface updates and dated patch summaries. Keep your existing folder and personal settings.</p><a href=\"launcher.html\">Update before playing →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"updates\">Keep up with changes</h2><p>Read <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Recent changes</a> for dated updates. Each release review covers affected guides, commands, item and zone pages, and this Features overview together.</p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> are available from all seven entrance Keepers. Existing legacy runs keep their original behavior until expiry or reset. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Not released:</strong> Removing the EXP penalty from normal death is prepared for approval. It is not active yet. <a href=\"unreleased.html#death-exp\">See the candidate details.</a></p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Not released:</strong> Separate cooldowns for the six basic Monk attacks are prepared. Dragon Punch/Tail Rake, Eagle Strike, Flying Kick, Kick, Round Kick and Tiger Claw will each keep their own reuse time. <a href=\"unreleased.html#monk-cooldowns\">See the candidate details.</a></p>",
