-  "body": "<h2 id=\"death-exp\">No EXP penalty on normal death</h2><p><strong>Not released.</strong> The tested candidate keeps normal EXP, AA progress and level intact through normal death. Existing buff loss and other death rules remain; prior EXP losses are not refunded. Production activation and in-game checks are pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"reforging\">Normal items in the Reforging Box</h2><p>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three-identical-Normal-to-Polished recipe</a> is implemented and regression-tested for eligible ordinary gear and zone-hunt rewards. Deployment and in-game acceptance are pending. Higher box upgrades retain their four-copy cost; dungeon rewards remain separate.</p>\n<h2 id=\"journal\">Adventure Journal &amp; Epic 0.5</h2><p>The eight journal quests and Wayfarer’s Oath charm have been built but are <strong>not installed on the server</strong>. The candidate uses three shared chapters followed by Guardian, Striker, Arcanist, Warden or Binder paths. These are not available rewards.</p><h2 id=\"combat\">Combat and item candidates</h2><p>Broader Monk and Beastlord fist-damage formulas and some existing tiered item corrections have a tested candidate but no recorded deployment. A frozen personal casting bar remains under investigation. The separate <a href=\"multiclass.html#earned-skills\">extra-class skill, trainer and offhand correction</a> is deployed; the reported player issue was confirmed resolved.</p>\n<h2 id=\"testing\">Ongoing checks for deployed features</h2><p>Broader equipment and class combinations, stats, regeneration, ability names and Bard movement/songs still need player checks. Those are acceptance checks for installed systems, not a claim that all of them are unreleased. See <a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> for the available systems.</p>\n",
+  "body": "<h2 id=\"monk-cooldowns\">Independent Monk attack cooldowns</h2><p><strong>Not released.</strong> A tested client/server correction gives Dragon Punch (Tail Rake for Iksar), Eagle Strike, Flying Kick, Kick, Round Kick and Tiger Claw their own cooldowns when you hold Monk. Using one will no longer lock the others. Each attack keeps its reuse duration, haste and earned AA adjustments; level, skill, target and range requirements still apply. Deployment and in-game combat and balance checks are pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"death-exp\">No EXP penalty on normal death</h2><p><strong>Not released.</strong> The tested candidate keeps normal EXP, AA progress and level intact through normal death. Existing buff loss and other death rules remain; prior EXP losses are not refunded. Production activation and in-game checks are pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"reforging\">Normal items in the Reforging Box</h2><p>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three-identical-Normal-to-Polished recipe</a> is implemented and regression-tested for eligible ordinary gear and zone-hunt rewards. Deployment and in-game acceptance are pending. Higher box upgrades retain their four-copy cost; dungeon rewards remain separate.</p>\n<h2 id=\"journal\">Adventure Journal &amp; Epic 0.5</h2><p>The eight journal quests and Wayfarer’s Oath charm have been built but are <strong>not installed on the server</strong>. The candidate uses three shared chapters followed by Guardian, Striker, Arcanist, Warden or Binder paths. These are not available rewards.</p><h2 id=\"combat\">Combat and item candidates</h2><p>Broader Monk and Beastlord fist-damage formulas and some existing tiered item corrections have a tested candidate but no recorded deployment. A frozen personal casting bar remains under investigation. The separate <a href=\"multiclass.html#earned-skills\">extra-class skill, trainer and offhand correction</a> is deployed; the reported player issue was confirmed resolved.</p>\n<h2 id=\"testing\">Ongoing checks for deployed features</h2><p>Broader equipment and class combinations, stats, regeneration, ability names and Bard movement/songs still need player checks. Those are acceptance checks for installed systems, not a claim that all of them are unreleased. See <a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> for the available systems.</p>\n",
